{
  "author_note": "Independent adversarial stand-in set, 40 claims, 10 per notice (26007 Ambiano pressure cookers, refund with cut-cord photo; 26244 Aroeve MK04 air purifiers, replacement, serial prefix BN and manufactured before July 2025; 24082 Justin SE4570 work boots, replacement, date code 07/22 NH or 08/22 NH; 25206 HONEYJOY high chairs, refund with RECALLED written on the seatback). Written from outcome_policy.yaml (including Revision 2 photo_rules) and the four notice texts only; no golden set, generator, label file, or code was read. Outcome mix: 16 approve, 9 deny, 7 needs_info, 8 flag. Conventions and assumptions: (1) None of the four notices requires a receipt, so no_receipt_when_required never fires and receipt_photo is varied on purpose, including false on approvals. (2) 26244 and 24082 are replacement remedies with no destruction instruction, so destruction_photo is 'none' on all their claims and never decides an outcome; refund_dollars is null for them. (3) 26007 and 25206 have no serial or date-code range, so their date codes are informational only (S02 has a 2015 date code with an in-window purchase, which must not be read as a window violation). (4) Purchase after the sale window has no policy rule; it appears once (S16), where a date-code violation decides the outcome. (5) Duplicate pairs: same_label_photo_as and same_address_as are set on the later spec of each pair only (S10 to S09, S30 to S29, S20 to S19, S40 to S39); both members of every pair are expected to be flag. S40 writes S39's address with 'Ln' for 'Lane' to test address normalization. (6) Label lines are given in full even when quality is 'unreadable'; the renderer should blur or degrade them until no character is legible. (7) Every label photo has distinct lines except the two designated reuse pairs. RENDERER REQUIREMENT: destruction and receipt photos must also be unique per spec (for example seeded by spec_id); if every 'destroyed' photo of a notice renders identically, duplicate_photo would fire on every claim and the expected outcomes no longer hold. Label line formats are invented where the notice does not fix one: 26007 'DATE CODE YYYY-MM', 26244 'S/N: BN...' and 'MFG DATE: MM/YYYY', 24082 'STYLE SE4570', 'SIZE ...', 'MM/22 NH', 25206 'DATE OF MFG: YYYY/MM'. 'destroyed' means: 26007, the unplugged power cord visibly cut through; 25206, the seat removed and 'RECALLED' in large marker letters on the seatback (front and rear). 'intact' means: 26007, the cooker with an uncut cord; 25206, the removed seat with no writing on it. All people, emails (example.com), streets, and city names are fictional.",
